---
description: Red-green TDD when implementing a feature or fix — skip a test only if you say why
alwaysApply: false
---

# TDD

When implementing a feature or a bug fix: failing test first, watch it fail, then write the code. Do not claim green without a fresh run. Delete code written before the test existed.

Prefer no test over a bad test. If you skip, say why in one sentence.

No hypothesis about a bug until a command already goes red on that bug.

Throwaway scripts, generated files, and config-only edits are exempt.
